# Last-handled neat-core version.
#
# Rebase consumes neat-core via an unpinned `path` dependency that tracks head.
# CI (`scripts/check-neat-core-version.sh`) fails when the sibling neat-core
# presents a breaking bump above this baseline — pre-1.0 a higher minor, or any
# higher major — forcing a deliberate upgrade. Clear the gate by updating
# `rebase` for the breaking change and bumping this version to match neat-core.
#
# 0.10.6 is the first version Rebase was written against: it keys synapse
# uniqueness by (fromUUID, toUUID, type), which is what the Forest adapter's
# `typed-pair` correction into an `IF` anchor emits.
#
# 0.10.6 -> 0.18.0 (Issue #110): acknowledge the seven pre-1.0 minor bumps core
# shipped while this gate went unexercised (Develop CI last ran 2026-08-29).
# 0.11.0 (core #619) added the `prune_*` modules — additive. 0.12.0 (core #633)
# made every `CompiledNetwork` field private behind accessors. 0.13.0 was the
# security-scan roll-up. 0.14.0 (core #640) bounds a creature's declared
# observation width (`validate_creature_width`, `CreatureError::TooManyNodes`).
# 0.15.0 (core #653) added `NetworkError::InvalidInputCount`, breaking only an
# exhaustive `match`. 0.16.0 / 0.17.0 widened the pruning bias-fold rule in
# `prune_neuron` / `prune_synapse`. 0.18.0 (core #684, Ockham #201) drives the
# pruning corner cases across the JSON / WASM boundary and adds
# `impl From<&PruneResult> for PruneResponse` — additive. Rebase names none of
# those items: it reaches
# core through `CreatureExport` / `NeuronExport` / `SynapseExport`,
# `parse_creature_json`, `creature_to_json*`, `creature_validate`,
# `compile_creature` and `training_data::{TrainingDataConfig, find_bin_files}`,
# all unchanged, so no Rebase source change was required. Verified against the
# sibling clone at core Develop 0.18.0 (0e2b0d6): `cargo clippy --workspace
# --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, `cargo fmt --all -- --check`
# and `cargo test --workspace --all-features` (158 lib tests + every
# integration target) are green with no edit.
#
# 0.18.0 -> 0.22.4 (PR #112): the weekly cargo-upgrade lockfile bump met core
# at 0.20.0 and tripped this gate; core Develop had reached 0.22.4 by the time
# it was handled, so the baseline moves to what CI checks out. Four pre-1.0
# minor bumps, per core's RELEASING.md. 0.19.0 (core #682) adds
# `CreatureError::UnknownTargetUuid` and makes `compile_creature` refuse a
# synapse whose `toUUID` names no listed neuron instead of dropping it.
# Rebase does not match on `CreatureError`, and `validate_creature` runs
# `creature_validate` before `compile_creature`, which already refuses a
# dangling endpoint as a topology error, so the new refusal is never the one
# that speaks. 0.20.0 (core #680) and 0.21.0 (core #698) are recorded by core
# as no public-API or behaviour change. 0.22.0 (core #688) makes the prune
# entry points splice out `IDENTITY` pass-throughs and adds a field to
# `CleanupOptions`, `CleanupOutcome`, `PruneResult` and `PruneResponse`;
# Rebase constructs none of those and calls no prune entry point, so neither
# count reaches it. Verified against the sibling clone at core Develop 0.22.4
# (4f999a0): clippy, fmt and `cargo test --workspace --all-features` (158 lib
# tests + every integration target) are green with no source change.
0.22.4
